cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Orbweaver: finding coordinated promotion-abuse rings in transaction graphs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dwivedi
    given-names: Adarsh
    email: 23ucs509@lnmiit.ac.in
repository-code: "https://github.com/adarshcod30/Orbweaver"
url: "https://orbweaver-adarshcod30s-projects.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  A densest-subgraph pipeline for detecting coordinated promotion-abuse
  rings: multi-relation graph construction with rarity- and lift-weighted
  edges, gradient-boosted account scoring, a provably-approximate greedy
  peeling extractor, case-file evidence generation, anchored night-to-night
  ring tracking, a capacity-aware review policy, and a Fast Belief
  Propagation label-propagation alternative to the learned scorer. Built for
  the Razorpay AI Buildathon, Track 02.
keywords:
  - fraud-detection
  - graph-algorithms
  - anomaly-detection
  - densest-subgraph
  - payments
  - fintech
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-04"
